    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nvim :help (including `:help api`) has many \"pseudo headers\" that look like:\n\n```\nrange({spec})                                            *vim.version.range()*\n    Parses a semver |version-range| \"spec\" and returns a range object:  \n    ...\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nTreat right-aligned tags as `h4`? This is necessary so that \"flow\" layout doesn't join the lines. In the above example,\n\n- the `range({spec})...` line should be a `h4` heading.\n- the `Parses a semver...` line should start a new `block`.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Maybe `h4` would be a better fit?",
