            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "## Proposal\n\nDefine h4 \"tag heading\" line to require a TAB char in the whitespace before the trailing tag(s).\n\n    :[count]verb[ose] {command}<Tab><Tab><Tab>*:verb* *:verbose*\n\nWhy a Tab:\n\n- Supporting the \"2+ spaces\" option currently specified at `:help help-tag-heading` , require a custom scanner.\n- A gap token that must start with a Tab (`/\\t[\\t ]*/`) never fails partway, so single spaces are still skipped as `extras`.\n\nPrototype results (on `runtime/doc/`)\n\n- No new ERRORs.\n- Corpus tests pass unchanged.\n- Parse speed is unchanged; `parser.c` is ~11% bigger.\n- A line of only tags is not an h4 (the heading must start with text). `UPPERCASE<Tab>*tag*` at block start is still `h3`.\n\n### Patch\n\n```diff\n--- a/grammar.js\n+++ b/grammar.js\n@@ -41,14 +41,16 @@\n\n   conflicts: $ => [\n     [$._line_noli, $._line_cb, $._column_heading],\n+    [$._line_noli, $._line_cb, $._column_heading, $._h4_heading],\n+    [$.uppercase_name, $._uppercase_words],\n     [$._line_any, $._line_noli],\n     [$._column_heading],\n+    [$._column_heading, $._h4_heading],\n   ],\n\n   extras: () => [/[\\t ]/],\n\n-  // inline: ($) => [\n-  // ],\n+  inline: ($) => [$._atom_noli],\n\n   rules: {\n     help_file: ($) =>\n@@ -71,12 +73,13 @@\n       $._word_common,\n     ),\n\n-    _atom_noli: ($) => choice(\n+    _atom_noli: ($) => choice($.tag, $._atom_noli_notag),\n+    _atom_noli_notag: ($) => choice(\n       alias($.word_noli, $.word),\n       // XXX: treesitter (undocumented) prefers an immediate token (uppercase_name) to tie-break\n       // e.g. \"CTRL-W s\". So use immediate() here too, then rule order decides.\n       alias(token.immediate(_keycode), $.keycode),\n-      $._atom_common,\n+      $._atom_notag,\n     ),\n     // Word NOT matching (numbered) listitem.\n     word_noli: ($) => choice(\n@@ -86,9 +89,9 @@\n       $._word_common,\n     ),\n\n-    _atom_common: ($) =>\n+    _atom_common: ($) => choice($.tag, $._atom_notag),\n+    _atom_notag: ($) =>\n       choice(\n-        $.tag,\n         $.url,\n         $.optionlink,\n         $.taglink,\n@@ -154,7 +157,7 @@\n       repeat(choice(_uppercase_word, $._uppercase_char)),\n     ),\n     // Line (plaintext) can start with uppercase words; don't flag as \"invalid h3\".\n-    _uppercase_words: ($) => prec.left(-1, seq(\n+    _uppercase_words: ($) => prec.dynamic(-1, seq(\n       alias(token.immediate(_uppercase_word), $.word),\n       alias(repeat(choice(_uppercase_word, $._uppercase_char)), $.word),\n     )),\n@@ -203,6 +206,7 @@\n     _blank: () => field('blank', /\\n/),\n     line: ($) => choice(\n       $.column_heading,\n+      $.h4,\n       $._line_noli,\n     ),\n     // Listitem: consumes prefixed line and all adjacent non-prefixed lines.\n@@ -224,12 +228,12 @@\n     // Line content (incl. whitespace) is captured as a single atom.\n     line_code: () => choice(/\\n/, /[\\t ]+[^\\n]+\\n/),\n     _line_noli: ($) => choice(\n-      seq(choice($._atom_noli, $._uppercase_words), repeat($._atom), /\\n/),\n+      seq(choice($._atom_noli, $._uppercase_words), repeat($._atom_gap), /\\n/),\n       $._line_cb,\n     ),\n     // Line ending with a codeblock. Also a codeblock-only line abutting a listitem. #118\n     _line_cb: ($) => seq(\n-      optional(seq(choice($._atom_noli, $._uppercase_words), repeat($._atom))),\n+      optional(seq(choice($._atom_noli, $._uppercase_words), repeat($._atom_gap))),\n       $.codeblock,\n     ),\n\n@@ -241,13 +245,14 @@\n     // TODO: children should be $.word (plaintext), not $.atom.\n     column_heading: ($) => seq(\n       alias($._column_heading, $.heading),\n+      optional($._gap),\n       alias('~', $.delimiter),\n       token.immediate(/\\n/),\n     ),\n     // aliasing a seq exposes every item separately: create hidden rule and alias that\n     _column_heading: $ => prec.dynamic(1, seq(\n       choice($._atom_noli, $._uppercase_words),\n-      repeat($._atom)\n+      repeat($._atom_gap)\n     )),\n\n     h1: ($) =>\n@@ -270,10 +275,25 @@\n     h3: ($) =>\n       seq(\n         alias($.uppercase_name, $.heading),\n-        optional(seq(choice($.tag, alias($._not_tag, $.word)), repeat($._atom))),\n+        optional(seq(optional($._gap), choice($.tag, alias($._not_tag, $.word)), repeat($._atom))),\n         /\\n/,\n       ),\n\n+    // Heading 4 (\"tag heading\"): text, then tags after whitespace containing a Tab, e.g.\n+    // \":verb[ose] {command}<Tab>*:verb* *:verbose*\". |help-tag-heading|\n+    h4: ($) => prec.dynamic(1, seq(\n+      alias($._h4_heading, $.heading),\n+      $._gap,\n+      $.tag,\n+      repeat(seq(optional($._gap), $.tag)),\n+      /\\n/,\n+    )),\n+    // Starts with text: \"<Tab>*a*<Tab>*b*\" is a line of tags.\n+    _h4_heading: ($) => seq(choice($._atom_noli_notag, $._uppercase_words), repeat($._atom_gap)),\n+    // Tab, then any whitespace: a token, so the grammar can see it (spaces alone are `extras`).\n+    _gap: () => token(/\\t[\\t ]*/),\n+    _atom_gap: ($) => choice($._atom, $._gap),\n+\n     // Tag: *foo* (see _not_tag).\n     tag: ($) => _word($, _tag_text, '*', '*'),\n\n```\n\n",
            "created_at": "2026-10-17T15:42:05Z",
